alk a  little bit about where in the world we  can look to for results about models  that are sort of in the style of what's  being done in Vancouver I mean I know  colloquially people often like to talk  about Portugal and sometimes will  incorrectly hear policy ascribed to  Portugal that's not exactly accurate so  sort of like what other models around  the world are there that are relevant  here well Portugal is a good one for us  to look to that's where they implemented  decriminalization over a decade ago but  like you said I agree with you it's not  a perfect comparison for North America  right now but that's Portugal has never  had to deal with fentanyl and like we  were saying a minute ago  decriminalization would not remove that  nor from organized crime so but there  are other there's other aspects or the  Portugal story that I think we should  look at when they decriminalized drugs  when they in some people's minds made  reviews more acceptable drug use did not  increase drug use decreased overdose  deaths decreased the spread of HIV  decreased and so the Portugal story is  not perfect but I bet I think we can't  look to it because there's a lot of  successes there we've been speaking with  Travis Lubich he's an award-winning  journalist also author of the book  fighting for space how a group of drug  users transformed one city's struggle  with addiction Travis really great work  and I really appreciate you talking to  me today thank you so much for having me  on

